    "multi_column_BzWAwD": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "item_4gjMPR": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrThomasStaudacher_b21450e1-b583-4742-b28b-e2d8bab47eb6.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Thomas Staudacher",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>N.D, LifePharm Scientific Advisory Board Member</h6><p>Thomas Staudacher has worked in the field of holistic medicine since graduating from the Germany-based Paracelsus School of Naturopathy in 2003. The Australian-based naturopathic doctor founded a relaxation technique called Acoustic Restoration Therapy™ and currently runs both the International Holistic Clinic of Natural Medicine and Subtle Energy Solution. Staudacher received advanced diplomas in naturopathy, nutrition, acupuncture, and homeopathy from the Australian Institute <br/>of Applied Science in Brisbane.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_w6kdWr": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Kimberly-Headshot_aa8fed86-7d37-4ae8-bb7e-3edd42d1b385.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Kimberly Purdy Lloyd",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>Executive Research and Development Scientist</h6><p>Extensive and ongoing research is an absolute necessity for LifePharm. Kimberly Purdy Lloyd has a career path of formidable experience in dietary supplement and specialty skincare formulations. She joined the Dietary Supplement industry with specialties in Wound Care and Cosmetic Formulations, developing clinical and basic research protocols and peer publishes results.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_xxqxaD": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrSamina-Headshot-2025_b09c7e84-c2fe-48ae-af53-68ebfc44c93e.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Samina Ahmad",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<h6>M.D., HHC, ALC, AP & AFNC, <br/>LifePharm Scientific Advisory Board Member</h6><p>While working as an Internal Medicine Physician, Dr. Samina Ahmad championed efforts for underprivileged Pakistani women and children. She is a strong advocate for better healthcare and nutrition in underserved countries. She received her medical degree from the University of Punjab in Pakistan and holds numerous certifications. Currently, she operates Samina’s Wellness in New York.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_wKjpCB": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrGiuseppe-Maffi_14952567-603b-479a-8be2-6108564e2f61.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Giuseppe Maffi",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>Ph.D, N.D, Scientific Advisory Board Member</h6><p>Dr. Giuseppe Maffi is a biologist and naturopath specializing in mitochondrial health, oxidative stress, and epigenetic therapies. With over 20 years of experience, he has advised leading nutraceutical and biotech companies on product development, scientific strategy, and regulatory affairs. A founding member of the Well Aging Project Society, Dr. Maffi is also a frequent speaker and published expert in the field of anti-aging and redox science. </p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_aFXXhX": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrSewiteNegash_92006159-371e-42af-bd85-2aca948becaf.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Sewite M. Negash",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>Ph.D, NIH, Science Advisory Board Member</h6><p>Dr. Sewite M. Negash got her Ph.D. in Biochemistry & Biophysics from the University of Kansas and did her post-doctoral training at the National Institutes of Health (NIH) and at the Pacific Northwest National Labs. She teaches college level biotechnology, chemistry and biochemistry courses, and her primary interest lies in understanding the interplay between chronic inflammation, oxidative stress, and the body’s anti-oxidant protection systems in health and disease. She has been published in numerous peer-reviewed journals. Through her philanthropic work, she advocates for access to free, quality education for all in Africa.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_RpGAxW": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrFrigyesBaack_a3c6df6c-b7bd-40ce-9e57-3619a69d902f.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Frigyes Back",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>Scientific Advisory Board Member</h6><p>Dr. Frigyes Back is a highly experienced specialist in surgery and proctology with decades of service in traditional medicine. He earned his medical degree from Semmelweis University of Medicine in Budapest in 1975 and completed his surgical specialization in 1980.Dr. Back began his medical career as an assistant lecturer at the Surgical Clinic of the Postgraduate Medical Training Institute. Over the years, he gained valuable international experience in Austria and Germany, and held key positions at esteemed institutions such as the 3rd Surgical Clinic of Semmelweis University and István Hospital. He later served as Chief Medical Inspector at the National Health Insurance Fund.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_DXEDXa": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Yana_Etemadi.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Yana Etemadi",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>NC, Science Advisory Board Member</h6><p>The Russian native, who graduated with honors from Bauman College as a nutritionist for six years. At her Denver-based private practice, Food as Medicine, she teaches patients how to shop for the proper foods to optimize the gut microbiome and makes home pantry inspections. She first became convinced of this brain-gut relationship when her young son was diagnosed with autism and she learned how integral a child’s diet is to their behavior.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_THeDrk": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DrAndujar-Headshot_1ace2437-04e0-4f95-a29f-f9d4df3cf4c0.jpg",
            "column_size": "2",
            "title": "Dr. Edward Andujar",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<h6>Scientific Advisory Board Member</h6><p>Dr. Frigyes Back is a highly experienced specialist in surgery and proctology with decades of service in traditional medicine. He earned his medical degree from Semmelweis University of Medicine in Budapest in 1975 and completed his surgical specialization in 1980.Dr. Back began his medical career as an assistant lecturer at the Surgical Clinic of the Postgraduate Medical Training Institute. Over the years, he gained valuable international experience in Austria and Germany, and held key positions at esteemed institutions such as the 3rd Surgical Clinic of Semmelweis University and István Hospital. He later served as Chief Medical Inspector at the National Health Insurance Fund.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        }
      },
